.TH MOXY-SHOW-EFFECTIVE-MOXYFILE 1 "" "moxy"
.SH NAME
moxy-show-effective-moxyfile \- Print the effective merged moxyfile as canonical TOML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moxy show-effective-moxyfile
.RI [ --dir = STRING ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Merges the moxyfile hierarchy for the working directory (or --dir) and prints the result as one include-free moxyfile: fixed key order, sorted lists and servers, commands in array form. The same configuration always prints the same bytes. Header values keep their $VAR references — nothing is expanded — so the output is safe to write to disk. allow-tools and pass-tools are written as the hierarchy merged them, per tool at the lowest level any layer holds it. Rendering a directory also records, under resolved-moxins, the directory each moxin name resolves to in the current environment; rendering a file reproduces the record it carries. A spawner captures this at spawn time and hands it to a child moxy as MOXY_PARENT_MOXYFILE. See moxyfile(5) NARROWING.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dir
Directory to walk as if it were the working directory. Default: the working directory.
Default: 
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moxy (1)
